# Astravon DSL

[![License: Astravonic Sovereign License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-Astravonic%20Sovereign%20License-blue.svg)](./LICENSE)

> **Astravon DSL** is a new domain-specific language created by House Astravon for building the next generation of intelligent, secure, and sovereign systems.  
> It unifies **AI, blockchain, biotechnology, and simulation** development into one elegant syntax and runs on the **Astravon Virtual Machine (AVM)**.

---

## ✨ Vision

Astravon DSL is not just another language.  
It is the **sovereign tongue of computation** for the Astravon technological dynasty:

- **Unified Domains** – Write AI reasoning, blockchain contracts, DNA encoding, and simulation code in one language.
- **Sovereign Runtime** – Code runs on the Astravon Virtual Machine (AVM) for maximum determinism, security, and performance.
- **Security by Default** – Memory safety, ethical use constraints, and formal verification built into the toolchain.
- **AGI-Native** – Designed as the native reasoning language of Astravon AGI.

---

## 🗂 Project Structure

astravon-dsl/
├── Cargo.toml # Rust project manifest
├── README.md # Overview of Astravon DSL
├── LICENSE # Astravonic Sovereign License
│
├── src/ # Core source code
│ ├── main.rs # Entry point for Astravon compiler/interpreter
│ ├── lib.rs # Shared library code
│ ├── lexer/ # Lexical analysis
│ ├── parser/ # Syntax parsing
│ ├── ast/ # Abstract Syntax Tree definitions
│ ├── semantics/ # Type checking, symbol resolution
│ ├── codegen/ # Code generation (LLVM / Wasm)
│ ├── runtime/ # Astravon Virtual Machine (AVM)
│ └── stdlib/ # Astravon Standard Library
│
├── examples/ # Example Astravon DSL scripts
├── tests/ # Unit and integration tests
├── docs/ # Documentation + Astravon Scrolls
└── scripts/ # Build and helper scripts


---

## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites
- Rust 1.75+ (with `cargo`)
- LLVM (if you plan to use the LLVM backend)
- Wasmtime (if you plan to target WebAssembly)

### Build
```bash
cargo build

Run
cargo run examples/hello_world.avon

Test
cargo test

📖 Examples
// examples/hello_world.avon
print "Hello, Astravon!"
Run it:


cargo run examples/hello_world.avon
